    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "WNDF-AV-000048 - Microsoft Defender AV must audit persistence through WMI event subscription."
      info        : "This policy setting prevents malware from abusing WMI to attain persistence on a device.

Fileless threats employ various tactics to stay hidden, to avoid being seen in the file system, and to gain periodic execution control. Some threats can abuse the WMI repository and event model to stay hidden."
      solution    : 'Set the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Microsoft Defender Antivirus >> Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard >> Attack Surface Reduction >> Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules to \'Enabled\'.

Under the policy option \'Set the state for each ASR rule:\', then click \'Show\'.

Enter GUID \'e6db77e5-3df2-4cf1-b95a-636979351e5b\' in the \'Value Name\' column.

Enter \'2\' in the \'Value\' column.'
